Resolve the aspect's type-stub deps in the exec configuration.

`_types_keys` / `_types_values` carry the Python type-stub wheels that mypy
itself consumes, so they belong in the exec configuration alongside `_mypy_cli`
(which already sets `cfg = "exec"`), not in the target configuration.

Left in the target configuration they are resolved for whatever platform is
being built, which breaks cross-compilation outright: the aspect is applied to
every top-level target, so building for a target platform that the Python lock
file has no environment for fails during loading, before the aspect's own
suppression tags get a chance to apply. Building any C++ target for a Windows
target platform hits this.

Moving them exposes a second defect that has to be fixed with it. A dependency
listed in `types` takes the `continue` branch below, so it never reaches the
loop that records the output roots its files live under; the only root the
aspect saw for that repository came from the *stub* target instead. Those roots
are joined with the target's own import paths to build `MYPYPATH`, so once the
stub target resolves in the exec configuration the resulting entry points at an
exec-configuration path while the dependency's files are staged in the target
configuration, and mypy stops finding the package. Collect each dependency's
roots from that dependency, before the type-mapping check.

diff --git a/mypy/private/mypy.bzl b/mypy/private/mypy.bzl
--- a/mypy/private/mypy.bzl
+++ b/mypy/private/mypy.bzl
@@ -135,6 +135,17 @@
             depsets.append(dep[RulesPythonPyInfo].transitive_sources)
             depsets.append(dep[RulesPythonPyInfo].transitive_pyi_files)

+        # Collect generated roots before the type-mapping check below can skip
+        # this dep: these roots are joined with the target's own import paths,
+        # so each dep has to contribute the root its own files live under.
+        for file in dep.default_runfiles.files.to_list():
+            root = file.root.path
+            if root:
+                if dep.label.workspace_root.startswith("external/"):
+                    generated_dirs[root + "/" + dep.label.workspace_root] = 1
+                else:
+                    generated_dirs[root] = 1
+
         if PyTypeLibraryInfo in dep:
             types.append(dep[PyTypeLibraryInfo].directory.path + "/site-packages")
         elif dep.label in type_mapping:
@@ -153,14 +164,6 @@
         if MypyCacheInfo in dep:
             upstream_caches.append(dep[MypyCacheInfo].directory)

-        for file in dep.default_runfiles.files.to_list():
